"Figure caption: Systemic delivery of mRNA-LNPs targets diverse cardiac cell types post-ischemic injury.A. Schematic of experimental set-up showing genetic lineage tracing in both male and female littermate Ai9 mice (10 weeks old) using lipid nanoparticles (LNPs; DLin-MC3-DMA 50%: Cholesterol 38.5%:DSPC 10%:DMG-PEG-2000 1.5%) loaded with modified Cre recombinase-encoding mRNA (mRNA-LNPs), administered intravenously 1 h after ischemia reperfusion injury (IRI). Echocardiography was conducted approximately 24 h after LNP injection, and end-point analysis including lightsheet microscopy, histology and flow cytometry, 3-, 14- and 28 days after LNP injection. n = 12–7 mice/group. B. Light-sheet microscopy of an optically cleared heart 28 days post-IRI. n = 1. tdTomato expression localized to the coronary occlusion zone and extended to the apex shown in orange. C. 3D reconstruction of mRNA-LNP distribution. Translucent purple, red and gold objects indicate overall heart, non-myocytes and myocytes, respectively. D. Morphological segmentation of tdTomato+ non-myocytes, and E. cardiomyocytes. (For interpretation of the references to colour in this figure legend, the reader is referred to the web version of this article.)\n\nFigure caption: mRNA-LNP uptake by cardiac cell types following IRI.A. Confocal micrographs of cardiac Ai9 mouse heart cross-sections 3, 14 or 28 days post LNP injection. Magnified views show epicardial and sub-epicardial regions enriched for tdTomato+ cells. B. Confocal micrograph of Ai9 mouse heart sections 3 days after LNP injection. Tissue is stained for nuclei (DAPI), cell surfaces (wheat germ agglutinin; WGA) and endothelial cells (isolectin B4; IB4). Magnified views show tdTomato+ cells lining the vascular lumen major cardiac blood vessels (C.) and cardiomyocytes (D.) within the ischemic region. All images are representative of 6 similar images acquired from 4 animals. n = 4 biological replicates/group.\n\nFigure caption: High dimensional flow cytometric analysis of tdTomato+ non-myocytes after IRI.Flow cytometry analysis on cells isolated at 3 (n = 10 biological replicates), 14 (n = 7 biological replicates) and 28 (n = 5 biological replicates) days post-IRI, as well as Control (uninjured) (n = 6 biological replicates) groups. A. Gating strategy showing viable (DAPI−) and nucleated (Vybrant DyeCycle Green, VDG+) cells. B. UMAP of viable myeloid, fibroblasts, endothelial cells, T cells, B cells, Schwann cells, pericytes and smooth muscle cells. C. Gating strategy to identify tdTomato+ cells. D. UMAP showing tdTomato+ cells in each viable cell population. E. Quantification of flow cytometry analysis. Percentage of viable cells per population for control (no IRI), 3, 14 and 28 days after IRI. F. Percentage of tdTomato+ cells in each cell population. G. Percentage of tdTomato+ cells of total tdTomato cells. Values shown as mean ± SD. (For interpretation of the references to colour in this figure legend, the reader is referred to the web version of this article.)\n\nFigure caption: Assessment of dose timing kinetics on mRNA-LNP uptake in non-myocytes.A. Schematic of experimental set-up showing genetic lineage tracing in both male and female littermate Ai9 mice (10 weeks old) using lipid nanoparticles (LNPs; DLin-MC3-DMA 50%: Cholesterol 38.5%: DSPC 10%: DMG-PEG-2000 1.5%) loaded with modified Cre mRNA (mRNA-LNPs), given 1 h (n = 3 mice) and 3 days (n = 4 mice) intravenously after ischemia reperfusion injury (IRI). End-point analysis of flow cytometry 28 days after IRI + LNP.Quantification of flow cytometry analysis on cells isolated from mice 28 days after mRNA-LNPs were administered 1 h (n = 3) and 3 days (n = 4) post-IRI. Percentage of tdTomato+ cells in each cell population: B. Fibroblasts, pericytes, Schwann Cells (Schw. cells) and smooth muscle cells (SMCs). C. Myeloid cells, B cells and T cells. D. Endothelial cells (ECs). Percentage of tdTomato+ cells of total tdTomato cells: E. Fibroblasts, pericytes, Schwann Cells (Schw. cells) and smooth muscle cells (SMCs). F. Myeloid cells, B cells and T cells. G. Endothelial cells (ECs). Values shown as min to max with mean ± SD. **p = 0.05 and **p = 0.01 determined by 2-way ANOVA with Sidak's multiple comparison test."